# OPERATIONS §2.3 (M3): with a base that loads, each refused scenario file's `scenario <s>: refused: …` line, as run
# prints it (§2.1), and no `ok`: exit 1. The reality of L6_4_scenario_isolated: child's version is named ola, also a
# key (LOAD-KEY), so child and twins (over it) are refused (L §6.4, §8). c2 (in child) and t1 (in twins) are asks
# in a refused scenario's world: their scenario's line covers them, and they print nothing. c1 is the base's.
=== options check exit=1
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2030-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
kind gifts: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input gift_amt: money PLN
input gift_dom: int

move gift[m in months, p in persons on day_of(m, gift_dom)]: gifts
  on day_of(m, gift_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount gift_amt

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ana] lives 1990-04-02..
  gift_amt = 100.00 PLN "own"
  gift_dom = 5 "own"
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask c1: count(p in persons on 2027-06-01)
ask c2: count(p in persons on 2027-06-01) in child
=== child.tally
scenario child over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01
  note "a child in March 2027"

input benefit_amt: money PLN
move benefit[m in months, p in persons on day_of(m, gift_dom)]: gifts
  on day_of(m, gift_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  when p == ola
  leg cash from world to konto amount benefit_amt

version ola
  cite plan
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-10-15
  persons + [ola] lives 2027-03-01..
  benefit_amt = 50.00 PLN "benefit act"
=== twins.tally
scenario twins over child
  tally 2
  from 2028-01-01

version ela_born
  cite plan
  governs 2028..
  known 2026-10-20
  persons + [ela] lives 2028-02-01..
  replace benefit_amt = 80.00 PLN "benefit act, two children"

ask t1: bal(konto, 2028-12-31), bal(konto, 2028-12-31) as if {scenario child} in twins
=== expect
scenario child: refused: LOAD-KEY a key is also an id: ola (child.tally:17)
scenario twins: refused: LOAD-KEY a key is also an id: ola (child.tally:17)
